  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "The Czech Republic (or Czechia), a landlocked Central European nation with a population of ~10.8 million, is a parliamentary democracy featuring a rich history of castles and UNESCO sites. The capital, Prague, is the largest city. The official language is Czech, and the currency is the Czech Crown (CZK).Key Information & FactsCapital and Major Cities: Prague is the capital; other major cities include Brno, Ostrava, Plzeň (Pilsen), and Liberec.Currency: Czech Koruna (CZK).Official Language: Czech.Government: Parliamentary republic with a president as head of state and a prime minister as head of government.Geography: Located in Central Europe, bordered by Germany, Austria, Slovakia, and Poland.History: Formed as an independent state in 1993 following the peaceful dissolution of Czechoslovakia.Travel & Visa InformationEntry Requirements: The Czech Republic is a member of the EU and the Schengen Area. Citizens from many countries (including the US, UK, and Canada) can enter for tourism without a visa for up to 90 days, though a European Travel Information and Authorization System (ETIAS) authorization will be required in the future for visa-exempt travelers.Currency Info: While in the EU, the country does not use the Euro, employing the Czech Crown (CZK) instead.Best Time to Visit: Spring (May) and fall (September) offer the best weather, while summer is popular but crowded, and winter is ideal for Christmas markets and skiing.Key Attractions: Prague Castle, Charles Bridge, Old Town Square, Cesky Krumlov, and countless other historic castles and spas.CultureBeer: Known for its beer culture, specifically the invention of Pilsner-style lager.Famous People: Franz Kafka, Antonín Dvořák, and Václav Havel.",
